-- title:
--   Convergent q-expansion tends to its constant term at i∞
-- statement:
--   Let $h$ be a real number with $0 < h$, let $F \colon \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be an arbitrary function on the upper half-plane, and let $(c_m)_{m \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of complex numbers. Assume that for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$ the series $\sum_{m \ge 0} c_m\, q^m$, where $q = \mathrm{qParam}\,h\,\tau = e^{2\pi i \tau / h}$ is Mathlib's $q$-parameter of period $h$, is summable with sum exactly $F(\tau)$ (the hypothesis is `HasSum`, i.e. unconditional summability of the family indexed by $m \in \mathbb{N}$ together with the identification of its sum with $F(\tau)$; no hypothesis of local uniformity or of holomorphy of $F$ is imposed). The conclusion is that $F$ converges to $c_0$ along the filter `UpperHalfPlane.atImInfty`, the filter generated by the sets on which $\operatorname{Im} \tau$ exceeds a given bound: that is, $F(\tau) \to c_0$ as $\operatorname{Im} \tau \to \infty$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a function on the upper half-plane given by a convergent $q$-expansion of period $h$ is holomorphic-at-the-cusp-style bounded at $i\infty$, with limiting value the constant term $c_0$; in particular such an $F$ is bounded near $i\infty$. It is used in the treatment of Siegel units and in the estimates bounding slashed modular functions in terms of $q$-parameters.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_tendsto_atImInfty_of_hasSum_qParam.lean

import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.Exp
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.Manifold
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.FunctionsBoundedAtInfty

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.tendsto_atImInfty_of_hasSum_qParam (h : ℝ) (hh : 0 < h) (F : UpperHalfPlane → ℂ) (c : ℕ → ℂ) (hc : ∀ τ : UpperHalfPlane, HasSum (fun m : ℕ => c m * Function.Periodic.qParam h (τ : ℂ) ^ m) (F τ)) : Filter.Tendsto F UpperHalfPlane.atImInfty (nhds (c 0)) := by sorry
